.UPDATE...
Issued at 830 AM PDT Fri Jul 24 2026

Once again, the dry air mass above the marine layer was able to mix
down and limit the coverage of stratus. This is the result of the
deepening mid/upper level through off of the Pacific Northwest
Coast. As stratus that has developed retreats to the coast, mostly
sunny skies are forecast regionwide this afternoon. Temperatures
will warm into the 60s to lower 70s in the west/northwest facing
locations near the coast, 70s to lower 80s across the bayshore and
Santa Cruz region, 80s to lower 90s across the interior, and mid-to-
upper 90s across the warmest spots in the interior Central Coast.
Overall, similar weather conditions regionwide as yesterday.

RGass

